[{"result": {"revisionguid": "00001027-a5dc-4f10-b178-30bf59ffe649", "comment": "", "creationdate": "2013-11-08 08:10:48.11", "contentlicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "posthistorytypeid": "2", "text": "You can't really even compare the two since the Kolmogorov-Smirnov is for a completely specified distribution (so if you're testing normality, you must specify the mean and variance, they can't be estimated from the data\*), while the Shapiro-Wilk is for normality, with unspecifed the mean and variance.

\* you also can't scale by parameter estimates and test for standard normal.

